  unsupported_claim.
- A directly_supported_fact must cite at least one segment id. If the material
  does not support it, it is an interpretation, a hypothesis or an opinion —
  say so rather than promoting it.
- Cite segment ids exactly as given above. Never invent an id, and never cite a
  segment that was not shown to you.
- Set qualification_required when a claim is true only under conditions the
  article would have to state (one measurement, one environment, one workload).
- Record anything the material marks as internal or unpublishable as a
  publication constraint, with the reason.
- Lessons and potential arguments reference claims by their claim id.
